From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] identify native riscv64 hosts as lnxriscv64

dev/make/identify_os.sh only knows x86_64 and aarch64, so on a native
riscv64 Linux host it prints "Unknown architecture: riscv64". The
lnxriscv64 build is otherwise complete (dev/make/function_definitions/
lnxriscv64.mk, compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk), but upstream
CI only builds it cross-compiled from x86_64, where the host identifies
as lnx32e and the gap is never hit. Natively, two things break:

- `make daal PLAT=lnxriscv64` fails in _release_nuspec, because
  deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh calls identify_os.sh itself and has
  no lnxriscv64 branch either:

      ./deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh: line 56: [: too many arguments
      Unknown platform Unknown architecture: riscv64
      make: *** [makefile:1109: _release_nuspec] Error 1

- the makefile compares PLAT against IDENTIFIED_PLAT to set
  COMPILER_is_cross, so a native build is treated as a cross build and
  clang is given --target=riscv64-linux-gnu instead of its host triple.

Map riscv64 to lnxriscv64 in identify_os.sh, and give
prepare_dal_nuget.sh a lnxriscv64 branch mirroring lnxarm with the
lib/riscv64 release directory the makefile already uses
(ARCH_DIR_ONEDAL = riscv64).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; upstream CI only cross-compiles lnxriscv64 from x86_64, so this native-host fix needs raising on its own]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh b/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
--- a/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
+++ b/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
@@ -67,6 +67,13 @@ create_package() {
         dynamic_lib_path=lib/arm
         static_lib_path=lib/arm
         lib_prefix=libonedal
+    elif [ ${platform} = "lnxriscv64" ]; then
+        platform=linux
+        tbb_platform=linux
+        rls_prefix=${rls_dir}/daal/latest
+        dynamic_lib_path=lib/riscv64
+        static_lib_path=lib/riscv64
+        lib_prefix=libonedal

     elif [ ${platform} = "mac32e" ]; then
         platform=osx-x64
diff --git a/dev/make/identify_os.sh b/dev/make/identify_os.sh
--- a/dev/make/identify_os.sh
+++ b/dev/make/identify_os.sh
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@ if [ "${os}" = "Linux" ]; then
     echo lnx32e
   elif [ "${ARCH}" = "aarch64" ]; then
     echo lnxarm
+  elif [ "${ARCH}" = "riscv64" ]; then
+    echo lnxriscv64
   else
     echo "Unknown architecture: ${ARCH}"
     exit 1
